data: {"text":"1. The Applicant most respectfully submits that he apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 142/2026 dated 18.04.2"}

data: {"text":"026, registered at PS Doranda, under Sections 318(4) and 336(3) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023."}

data: {"text":" The Applicant has not been arrested yet but seeks anticipatory bail in view of the apprehension of arrest in"}

data: {"text":" the aforesaid case.\n\n2. The Applicant submits that he apprehends arrest in connection with FIR No. 142/2026"}

data: {"text":" dated 18.04.2026 lodged at PS Doranda, Ranchi, wherein he has been fals"}

data: {"text":"ely implicated. The said FIR has been lodged on the basis of a false and frivolous complaint by the de-facto complainant arising out of a commercial partnership dispute involving a transport business.\n\n3. The Applicant subm"}

data: {"text":"its that he is a well-known transporter in Ranchi and has been carrying on his legitimate business activities for several"}

data: {"text":" years. The present case is nothing but a result of a commercial dispute between business partners which"}

data: {"text":" has been given a criminal colour to har"}

data: {"text":"ass and humiliate the Applicant.\n\n4. The Applicant further submits that he undertakes to cooperate fully with the investigation and shall not leave the territorial jurisdiction of Jharkhand without prior permission of this"}

data: {"text":" Hon'ble Court. The Applicant is ready and willing to join the investigation as and when called upon by"}

data: {"text":" the investigating agency.\n\n5. The Applicant submits that he has been falsely implicated in the present case and the allegations"}

data: {"text":" levelled against him are completely baseless and without any substance. The matter is purely civil"}

data: {"text":" in nature arising out of business disputes between partners and does not involve any criminal liability on"}

data: {"text":" the part of the Applicant.\n\n6. The Applicant submits that the dispute is essentially of a civil nature pert"}

data: {"text":"aining to partnership business dealings and financial transactions. The complainant, being ag"}

data: {"text":"grieved by certain commercial decisions, has resorted to filing a criminal complaint to"}

data: {"text":" pressurize the Applicant and gain undue advantage in the civil dispute"}

data: {"text":".\n\n7. The Applicant respectfully submits that he has no criminal antecedents and has never been involved in any criminal case whatsoever. He is a resp"}

data: {"text":"ectable member of society and has always conducted himself in accordance with law"}

data: {"text":". His reputation and standing in the community is impeccable.\n\n8. The Applicant submits that he has"}

data: {"text":" deep roots in the community and has been residing in Ranchi for several decades. He has substantial business interests and immovable properties"}

data: {"text":" in Jharkhand. There is no question of his fleeing from justice or evading the"}

data: {"text":" legal process.\n\n9. The Applicant submits that custodial interrogation is not necessary in the present case as he is willing to join the investigation and cooperate with"}

data: {"text":" the investigating agency. His liberty should not be curtailed when he is ready to make himself"}

data: {"text":" available for investigation as and when required.\n\n10. The Applicant respectfully relies upon the judgment of the Hon'ble Supreme Court in Sushila Ag"}

data: {"text":"garwal v. State (2020) 5 SCC 1, wherein it has been held that while considering anticip"}

data: {"text":"atory bail applications, the court must balance the freedom of the individual guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution with the interests of the society and the investigation."}

data: {"text":"\n\n11. The Applicant submits that his fundamental right to life and personal liberty as guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of"}

data: {"text":" India would be violated if he is arrested in this false and frivolous case. The conditions for"}

data: {"text":" grant of anticipatory bail as laid down by the Hon'ble Supreme Court are fully satisfied in the present case.\n\n12. The"}

data: {"text":" Applicant submits that the investigation is pending and no useful purpose would be served by arresting him when he has already assured"}

data: {"text":" full cooperation with the investigating agency. Grant of anticipatory bail would serve the ends of justice and prevent any misuse of the criminal"}

data: {"text":" law process."}

